# Normalise line endings in the REPOSITORY, so every platform checks out
# byte-identical sources.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The production Content-Security-Policy in
# `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` authorises the inline theme bootstrap in
# `index.html` by sha256 hash, and a hash is byte-exact: the same script
# hashes differently under LF and CRLF. GitHub's `windows-latest` runners
# set `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a Windows release would
# check out `index.html` with CRLF, `vite build` would copy those CRLF bytes
# into `dist/`, and the shipped app's CSP would no longer match its own
# inline script -- a blank window in production only, with a green local
# build. `src/lib/releaseIntegrity.test.ts` is what makes that visible.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF on every OS (LF in the repository,
# LF on disk), so the pinned hash is correct for macOS, Linux and Windows
# alike. `text=auto` keeps git's binary detection, so images and icons are
# never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never let line-ending conversion reach them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
